  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, up to a maximum amount of P10,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, this means that when calculating the estate tax, the value of the family home can be excluded from the total gross estate up to the specified limit. This deduction can significantly impact the overall estate tax due, making it an important consideration for estate planning and administration.",
